<article class="env-lemma" id="0G7T">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0G7T">Lemma <span data-tag="0G7T">36.6.13</span>.</a> Let $X$ be a scheme. Let $Z \to X$ be a closed immersion of finite presentation whose conormal sheaf $\mathcal{C}_{Z/X}$ is locally free of rank $c$. Then there is a canonical map </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  c : \wedge ^ c(\mathcal{C}_{Z/X})^\vee \otimes _{\mathcal{O}_ Z} i^*\mathcal{F} \longrightarrow \mathcal{H}_ Z^ c(\mathcal{F})  \]
</div>
  <p> functorial in the quasi-coherent module $\mathcal{F}$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Follows from the construction in Remark <a href="/tag/0G7Q" data-tag="0G7Q">36.6.10</a> and the independence of the choice of generators of the ideal sheaf shown in Lemma <a href="/tag/0G7S" data-tag="0G7S">36.6.12</a>. Some details omitted. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>